211 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 947 0 R
/E (This project focuses on building a real-time data processing pipeline using Apache Kafka and Apache Spark to perform word count analytics on streaming data. In today's digital world, real-time insights are crucial for many industries. By leveraging Kafka as the data ingestion platform and Spark for real-time data processing, this project demonstrates an efficient and scalable architecture for streaming applications. The work involves setting up a local development environment using Windows Subsystem for Linux \(WSL\), installing essential tools like Java, Python, and Spark, and developing a Python-based word count program that reads streaming data from a Kafka topic and processes it in real time. This project highlights the power of real-time big data frameworks and provides a fundamental implementation model for future real-world streaming solutions.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
