<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (In the age of digital transformation, organizations are generating massive volumes of data from various sources like social media, IoT devices, mobile apps, sensors, and transactions. While traditional batch processing is useful for analyzing large datasets over time, there's an increasing demand for real-time insights. This is where real-time data processing comes into play.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
438 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Real-time data processing refers to the continuous input, processing, and output of data with minimal latency. It allows businesses to analyze and act on data as soon as it is generated, enabling faster decision-making.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
